# Testing

Run headless suite:

```sh
love tests
```

Exit `0` = pass, `1` = fail. Config in `tests/conf.lua` disables window/audio.

## Structure

- `tests/framework.lua` — `describe`, `it`, `assert_equal`, etc.
- `tests/runner.lua` — auto-discovers `tests/unit/test_*.lua`
- `tests/helpers/mock_env.lua` — stubs `G`, loads real engine classes when needed

## New test template

```lua
local T = require("tests.framework")
local mock_env = require("tests.helpers.mock_env")

T.describe("feature", function()
    mock_env.reset_game()
    T.it("does thing", function()
        T.assert_equal(actual, expected)
    end)
end)
```

No manual registration in `runner.lua` — naming `test_*.lua` under `tests/unit/` is enough.

## Jumble-related tests

`test_jumble_patterns.lua`, `test_jumble_scoring.lua`, `test_jumble_play_flow.lua`, `test_letter_card_faces.lua`

Use `mock_env.ensure_engine_globals()` when tests need real `Sprite`/`Node`/`Card` classes.
